# SYNOPSIS

```usage
vx cpu -k nodekey [-r root] [-c command] [--key file] node
vx cpu --show-key [--key file]
```

# DESCRIPTION

`vx cpu` runs rc(1) on a node, as Plan 9's cpu does from a terminal: rc's terminal is this one, and the node sees this machine's files at `/mnt/term`.
It calls the node's cpu server (cpu(8)) at <node>, a host, `host!port` or `tcp!host!port`, port 17019 if none is given, and seals the call with Noise IK (noise(2)) as this terminal, expecting the node whose public key is <nodekey>, 64 hex digits.
The node's key is on its console, in the cpu server's line `cpu: listening on tcp!*!17019, key` <nodekey>; the handshake fails if the node holds another.
The node answers only the terminal whose key its image carries, which `vx boot --cpu` (vx-build(1)) puts there.

With `-c` rc runs <command> and ends; without it rc is interactive, prompting and reading lines until the end of input (^D).
The session ends when rc does, and `vx cpu` with it.

This terminal stays in cooked mode: it edits each line and sends it when it is typed, and nothing on either side is a pty.
^C is posted to rc's note group on the node as `interrupt`, which ends the program rc is running; it doesn't end `vx cpu`.

The tree `vx cpu` serves at the node's `/mnt/term` is laid out as drawterm lays out a host's that isn't Plan 9:

: `dev/cons`
  The terminal: a read waits for a line typed, and is empty at the end of input; a write is shown.
  The node's `/dev/cons` for the session is this file.
: `dev/cpunote`
  A read waits for a note: `interrupt` at each ^C.
: `root/`
  This machine's files, from <root> (`/` by default), read and written as the user running `vx cpu`.

`--key` names this terminal's key file, `$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/vectraos/cpu.key` (or `~/.config/vectraos/cpu.key`) by default: 32 random bytes, made the first time with only its owner allowed to read it.
`--show-key` prints the terminal's public key, what `vx boot --cpu` takes.

# EXAMPLES

Boot amd64 with a cpu server for this terminal, then, from another terminal, copy a file from the node to here:

```rc
% vx boot --cpu
...
cpu: listening on tcp!*!17019, key 5c3f...
```

```rc
% vx cpu -k 5c3f... -c 'cp /lib/man/1/rc /mnt/term/root/tmp/rc.1' localhost
```

